15 0 obj
<< /A 36 0 R /Alt (Panel A is a line chart comparing cumulative incidence of acute GvHD grades III\205IV over time in days for MRD, MUD, and Haplo stem cell sources, showing no significant difference \(p=0.85\). Panel B is a line chart of cumulative incidence of moderate and severe chronic GvHD over months, also showing no significant difference among the three groups \(p=0.57\). Panel C is a grouped bar chart indicating that a higher percentage of acute GvHD cases are associated with high CD4+ T cell counts \(p=0.04\) and low B cell counts \(p=0.03\), with red for GvHD cases and blue for no GvHD.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 37 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a line graph comparing non-relapse mortality over five years for MRD, MUD, and Haplo groups, with similar cumulative incidences and a pvalue of 0.30. Panel B displays non-relapse mortality, revealing higher cumulative incidence in the low B cell count group compared to the high B cell count group, with a significant p-value below 0.01. Panel C presents relapse/progressive disease \(PD\) rates among MRD, MUD, and Haplo groups, with no significant difference and a p-value of 0.31. Panel D demonstrates higher relapse/PD incidence in the low NK cell count group compared to the high NK cell count group, with a p-value of 0.03.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Figure contains six panels illustrating survival and cell recovery data after transplantation. Panels A\205D display Kaplan-Meier survival curves for disease-free survival, overall survival, graft-versus-host-disease-free/relapse-free survival, and chronic graft-versus-host-disease-free/relapse-free survival, comparing MRD, MUD, and Haplo groups with p-values above 0.3. Panels E\205F show bar charts of NK cell and B cell recovery, where higher cell recovery correlates with significantly improved disease-free and overall survival in most comparisons, with p-values of 0.04.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
